      {
        "id": 194326,
        "name": "KateWalker",
        "username": "TakeWalker",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/{size}/5677_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-03-30T22:10:41.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'm doing the \"play all villains with the new team\" thing, too (albeit with guest stars).</p><p>The one thing about Termi-Nation is they're all pretty slow and need a lot of setup. Absolute Zero is going to spend a lot of time skipping his power phase until he's good and ready to unleash frosty heck. Unity's card-draw is fantastic for her, but also means you'll have a lot of turns without any bots in play (not too different from how I usually play her, at least; and you can always Flash Forge something into the trash to put in play!) TN Bunker sets up a lot faster than his counterparts, but that's still pretty slow compared to many other heroes. (He's still one of the best Bunkers.)</p><p>So it takes a little patience, and if you're playing a villain who punishes patience, you might find yourself in a heap of trouble if you don't have anyone else to rely on. Still, Unity with a lot of setup is a monster, no matter who you're fighting (and TN AZ doubly so), so they can be rewarding!</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:21:27.585Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
