        "raw": "<p>I&#39;m doing the &quot;play all villains with the new team&quot; thing, too (albeit with guest stars).</p><p>The one thing about Termi-Nation is they&#39;re all pretty slow and need a lot of setup. Absolute Zero is going to spend a lot of time skipping his power phase until he&#39;s good and ready to unleash frosty heck. Unity&#39;s card-draw is fantastic for her, but also means you&#39;ll have a lot of turns without any bots in play (not too different from how I usually play her, at least; and you can always Flash Forge something into the trash to put in play!) TN Bunker sets up a lot faster than his counterparts, but that&#39;s still pretty slow compared to many other heroes. (He&#39;s still one of the best Bunkers.)</p><p>So it takes a little patience, and if you&#39;re playing a villain who punishes patience, you might find yourself in a heap of trouble if you don&#39;t have anyone else to rely on. Still, Unity with a lot of setup is a monster, no matter who you&#39;re fighting (and TN AZ doubly so), so they can be rewarding!</p>",
