      {
        "id": 194327,
        "name": "The Burning Stickman",
        "username": "The_Burning_Stickman",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_burning_stickman/{size}/2003_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-03-30T22:30:43.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The only real 'synergy' I see in them, because they don't really have much in the way of interaction built into their decks, is having Unity give AZ an extra power usage to boost his damage the net turn.</p><p>One neat trick I did once, though -- using them (with Legacy and TLT) against Apostate, and Unity was up, with AZ playing clean-up -- <i>but</i>&nbsp;AZ had used Violent Shivers last turn, had Cold Snap out, and there was a Relic Spirit on the board that he would've killed with it before getting a chance to finish off Apostate. Easily solved, however, by nuking Bee-Bot, taking out Cold Snap, smacking Apostate and putting a Platform Bot back into play.</p><p>Outside of that, though, there's very little in the way of interaction between them.</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:21:27.663Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
